The owner's post-launch review of Phase 1 above flagged five real gaps: portal mod cards navigated out
to the PUBLIC marketing page instead of a portal-chrome'd route, the shipped pages were a bare text list
next to the approved mockups (`.design-refs/nxlabs/*.png`), Modrinth's real `gallery[]` images were never
fetched, there was no real author credit, and ratings/comments/search/sort were entirely absent (all
previously listed above as "out of scope, deliberately" — now in scope).

**Schema additions** (`prisma/schema.prisma`): `GameMod.galleryUrls String[]` (real Modrinth project
gallery images, CDN-hosted), `GameMod.authorName`/`authorAvatarUrl` (real creator credit resolved from
the source, not the mod itself). New `ModRating` model — cuid id, real `userId` FK to `User`
(`onDelete: Cascade`), `rating Int` (1-5), optional `comment`, real `createdAt`/`updatedAt`, unique
`(userId, gameModId)`. One table backs BOTH the average-rating aggregate and the comment list (a comment
is just a `ModRating` row whose `comment` isn't null) — deliberately not split into two models, since the
brief's own "one rating + optional comment per user per mod" requirement already matches one row's shape
exactly, and splitting would let a user's rating and their comment drift out of sync. Not a fork of the
existing admin-only `Review` model (curated homepage testimonials, no `userId`, approved/featured
workflow) — this is unmoderated, customer-authored, per-mod feedback.

