(sorted featured-first, capped at 8) with zero extra API calls (already part of the `GET /v2/project/{id}`
response), and makes one extra call to `GET /v2/team/{id}/members` for the project owner's real username +
avatar. `verifySpigotmc` makes one extra call to `GET /v2/authors/{id}` to resolve the resource author's
real display name (Spiget's resource payload only carries the numeric id). `verifyThunderstore` uses the
package's real namespace as `authorName` (Thunderstore has no per-author avatar/bio endpoint). All three
author/gallery lookups are best-effort — a failure there costs only the credit/gallery, never the whole
verification pass (the project-level facts already succeeded by that point).

